dd-4c26-af80-7f527a952d26",1,"78131a59-245e-4945-85f0-1b7756c8840c",1,"INTERFACE (ITcVnImage)"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"1. Raw detector output","bounding":[584,62.29999542236328,4992.64013671875,837.6000366210938],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"A detector (for example a neural network) typically reports several overlapping boxes for each object, each with a confidence score. Here 9 candidates are entered by hand: 3, 2 and 3 boxes around the three nuts, plus a weak 0.30 hit on a smudge."},{"id":2,"title":"2. Show every candidate","bounding":[1304,970.300048828125,4562.64013671875,347.6000061035156],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"All 9 boxes drawn in yellow on a colour copy of the image."},{"id":3,"title":"3. Non-maximum suppression","bounding":[5608.64013671875,2102.2998046875,743.748046875,556.5999755859375],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"F_VN_NonMaxSuppression drops boxes scoring below fScoreThreshold (0.5, removes the smudge), then keeps the best-scoring box of each overlapping cluster: any box overlapping a better one by IoU >= fOverlapThreshold (0.5) is suppressed. It returns the indices of the kept boxes, best score first."},{"id":4,"title":"4. Draw the kept boxes","bounding":[1304,1388.300048828125,7112.568359375,643.5999755859375],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"Each kept index picks its box from the candidate list, drawn in green: one box per nut."}],"config":{},"extra":{"filemeta":{"name":"Remove Duplicate Detections with NonMaxSuppression","description":"This example shows how F_VN_NonMaxSuppression reduces a detector's overlapping candidate boxes to one box per object.","tags":["Pick and Place","Robotics","Object Detection","Counting"]},"__aiIds":{"554d4698-8274-4bff-bff1-5956e8bc45fc":"img","20b6c425-87cd-451b-9d33-d16a8ab6115e":"tR","acfaf961-4dfd-4578-8d47-b4eacdbf2dd7":"tS","aa2f04af-f32f-40c2-81a1-3f4b1ba57b12":"cR","c58d953a-a148-431f-9